><main class=\"flex-1 min-w-0 bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-200 p-6 md:p-8\"><header class=\"border-b border-gray-100 pb-6 mb-6\"><h1 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight tracking-tight\">Celebrating Eid al-Fitr 2026 in UAE: Prayer Timings, Traditions &amp; Free Events</h1><div class=\"flex items-center text-sm text-gray-500 gap-4\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><span class=\"font-semibold text-gray-900\">Last Updated:</span><time dateTime=\"2026-01-01T07:07:24Z\">1 January 2026</time></div></div></header><div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto font-sans\"><div class=\"relative w-full aspect-video md:aspect-21/9 rounded-xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm mb-8 bg-gray-100 border border-gray-100\"><img alt=\"Guide to celebrating Eid al-Fitr 2026 in UAE, featuring prayer timings, traditions, and free events in Dubai.\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"fill\" class=\"object-cover\" style=\"position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent\" src=\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/kxdjzy8e/production/0031138d49fac10d280490a7a39102672be815ab-1920x1080.webp\"/><div class=\"absolute top-4 left-4 bg-white/95 backdrop-blur-md px-3 py-2 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100 text-center min-w-15\"><span class=\"block text-xs font-bold text-red-600 uppercase tracking-wider\">Mar</span><span class=\"block text-xl font-black text-slate-900 leading-none mt-0.5\">20</span></div></div><div class=\"mb-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2 items-center\"><span class=\"inline-flex items-center bg-blue-50 text-blue-700 text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wider border border-blue-100\">UAE What&#x27;s On: Events, Public Holidays &amp; Festivals 2026</span></div><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 bg-slate-50 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/60 mb-8\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-4\"><div class=\"bg-white p-2.5 rounded-xl text-blue-600 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-calendar w-5 h-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M8 2v4\"></path><path d=\"M16 2v4\"></path><rect width=\"18\" height=\"18\" x=\"3\" y=\"4\" rx=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M3 10h18\"></path></svg></div><div><h2 class=\"font-bold text-gray-900 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-1\">Date &amp; Time</h2><p class=\"text-gray-900 font-semibold leading-tight\">Friday, 20 March 2026</p><p class=\"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-1\">Starts at <!-- -->04:30 AM</p></div></div><div class=\"flex items-start gap-4\"><div class=\"bg-white p-2.5 rounded-xl text-red-500 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-map-pin w-5 h-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 10c0 4.993-5.539 10.193-7.399 11.799a1 1 0 0 1-1.202 0C9.539 20.193 4 14.993 4 10a8 8 0 0 1 16 0\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"10\" r=\"3\"></circle></svg></div><div><h3 class=\"font-bold text-gray-900 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-1\">Location</h3><p class=\"font-semibold text-gray-900 leading-tight mb-0.5\">United Arab Emirates</p><p class=\"text-sm text-gray-500 leading-snug\">Dubai, AE</p></div></div></div><article class=\"prose prose-lg prose-headings:text-slate-900 prose-p:text-slate-700 prose-a:text-blue-600 prose-a:font-semibold prose-img:rounded-xl max-w-none\"><div class=\"mb-10 text-xl font-medium text-slate-800 leading-relaxed border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-6 py-1\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Eid al-Fitr 2026 is one of the most important Islamic holidays in the UAE, bringing together prayer, tradition, family visits, and festive public celebrations across Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Sharjah, and other emirates.</p></div><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Eid al-Fitr is one of the most anticipated celebrations in the UAE, marking the joyful conclusion of the holy month of Ramadan. In 2026, Eid is expected to fall in <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">late March</strong>, subject to the official moon sighting announced by UAE authorities.</p><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Across <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Sharjah, and other emirates</strong>, Eid al-Fitr brings together spirituality, family traditions, cultural heritage, and vibrant public celebrations. From early morning Eid prayers to free fireworks and community events, this guide helps you experience <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Eid al-Fitr 2026 in the UAE</strong> to the fullest.</p><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Eid al-Fitr 2026 Prayer Timings in the UAE (Expected)</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Eid prayer is performed shortly after sunrise on the first day of Eid. While final timings are confirmed only after the moon sighting, the following are <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">expected prayer times for Eid al-Fitr 2026</strong> across the UAE:</p><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Expected Eid Prayer Timings by Emirate</h3><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Abu Dhabi:</strong> 6:25 – 6:30 AM</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Dubai:</strong> 6:20 – 6:25 AM</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Sharjah:</strong> 6:18 – 6:23 AM</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Ajman:</strong> 6:18 AM</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Umm Al Quwain:</strong> 6:17 AM</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Fujairah:</strong> 6:15 AM</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Ras Al Khaimah:</strong> 6:15 AM</li></ul><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\"><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Important tips for worshippers:</strong></p><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li>Arrive <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">30–45 minutes early</strong></li><li>Follow updates from <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">UAE Awqaf / Islamic Affairs</strong></li><li>Check announcements from your local mosque</li></ul><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Where to Perform Eid Prayers in the UAE</h2><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Popular Eid Prayer Mosques in Dubai</h3><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li>Jumeirah Mosque</li><li>Grand Mosque, Bur Dubai</li><li>Al Farooq Omar Bin Al Khattab Mosque</li><li>Al Salam Mosque, Al Barsha</li></ul><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Best Eid Prayer Locations in Abu Dhabi</h3><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li>Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque</li><li>Mariam Umm Eisa Mosque</li><li>Al Kareem Mosque, Al Reem Island</li><li>Sheikh Sultan Bin Zayed The First Mosque</li></ul><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Well-Known Eid Mosques in Sharjah</h3><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li>King Faisal Mosque</li><li>Al Noor Mosque</li><li>Sharjah Grand Mosque</li><li>Al Maghfirah Mosque</li></ul><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Visitors planning to attend Eid prayers at <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque</strong> are advised to check official guidelines before arrival.</p><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">How Eid al-Fitr Is Celebrated in the UAE</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Eid al-Fitr in the UAE reflects the country’s deep-rooted Islamic values and strong sense of community.</p><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Eid Greetings and Social Traditions</h3><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Exchanging <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">“Eid Mubarak”</strong> greetings is a central part of the celebration, whether at mosques, homes, malls, or public spaces.</p><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Traditional Emirati Eid Food</h3><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Food plays a major role in Eid celebrations, with families preparing special dishes such as:</p><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li>Ouzi (slow-cooked lamb with spiced rice)</li><li>Luqaimat (sweet dumplings with date syrup)</li><li>Machboos (Emirati-style spiced rice)</li><li>Hashwa (rice with minced meat)</li><li>Kunafa (classic Eid dessert)</li></ul><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Many hotels and local restaurants across Dubai and Abu Dhabi introduce <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">special Eid menus</strong> during the holidays.</p><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Eidiya: A Special Moment for Children</h3><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Children receive <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Eidiya</strong>, a traditional cash gift from elders, symbolising generosity and joy. Shopping malls and community centres often organise kid-friendly Eid activities during this time.</p><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Family Visits and Gatherings</h3><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Eid al-Fitr is a time for family reunions, shared meals, gift exchanges, and strengthening bonds — a tradition deeply valued in Emirati culture.</p><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Free Eid al-Fitr 2026 Events and Activities in the UAE</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">One of the highlights of Eid in the UAE is the wide range of <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">free public events</strong> organised across the country.</p><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Eid Fireworks Displays</h3><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Dubai:</strong> Burj Khalifa area, Dubai Festival City, JBR</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Abu Dhabi:</strong> Yas Island, Abu Dhabi Corniche</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Sharjah:</strong> Al Majaz Waterfront</li></ul><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Public Beaches and Parks</h3><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li>Kite Beach, Dubai</li><li>Corniche Beach, Abu Dhabi</li><li>Al Mamzar Beach Park, Sharjah</li></ul><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Cultural Attractions with Free Entry</h3><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li>Al Fahidi Historical District, Dubai</li><li>Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque, Abu Dhabi</li><li>Sharjah Arts and Heritage Area</li></ul><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Free Eid Entertainment at Malls</h3><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li>Dubai Mall</li><li>Yas Mall, Abu Dhabi</li><li>City Centre Sharjah</li></ul><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Tips to Enjoy Eid al-Fitr 2026 in the UAE</h2><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li>Follow official UAE announcements for confirmed dates</li><li>Visit popular locations early to avoid crowds</li><li>Use public transport where possible</li><li>Respect cultural and religious customs</li></ul><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Why Eid al-Fitr in the UAE Is Truly Special</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Eid al-Fitr in the UAE is a unique blend of <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">faith, culture, and celebration</strong>. Whether you’re attending Eid prayers at a grand mosque, enjoying traditional Emirati food with family, or watching fireworks light up the skyline, Eid offers unforgettable moments for residents and visitors alike.</p><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\"><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\"><em>Eid Mubarak from all of us at TopTenUAE.com!</em></strong></p></article><div class=\"mt-16 pt-10 border-t border-gray-100\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 flex items-center gap-2\">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class=\"bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm overflow-hidden mb-12\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50/50\"><h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 flex items-center gap-3\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-circle-question-mark w-6 h-6 text-primary\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"></circle><path d=\"M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3\"></path><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"></path></svg>Frequently Asked Questions</h2></div><div class=\"divide-y divide-gray-100\"><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">When is Eid al-Fitr 2026 expected in the UAE?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Eid al-Fitr 2026 is expected in <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">late March</strong>, subject to the official moon sighting announcement.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">Where can I attend Eid prayers in the UAE?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Major mosques include Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque (Abu Dhabi), Jumeirah Mosque (Dubai), and King Faisal Mosque (Sharjah).</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">Are there free Eid events in the UAE?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Yes, including fireworks, cultural shows, public beaches, and mall entertainment.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">Can tourists participate in Eid celebrations?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Yes. Tourists are welcome to attend public events, visit mosques, and experience Eid traditions respectfully.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">What should I wear for Eid prayers?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Modest clothing is recommended, such as abayas for women and kanduras for men.</p></div></details></div></div></div></div></main><aside class=\"w-full lg:w-80 shrink-0 space-y-8 mt-12 lg:mt-0\"><div class=\"bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden\"><div class=\"absolute top-0 right-0 w-24 h-24 bg-primary/5 rounded-full translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2\"></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-4 mb-4 relative z-10\"><div class=\"w-14 h-14 bg-gray-50 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden border-2 border-white shadow-md\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-shield-check w-7 h-7 text-[#4b0082]\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z\"></path><path d=\"m9 12